topic('Async & Threading')
M('a','k',"What does the await keyword do in an async method?","Pauses the method without blocking the thread until the task completes","Starts a new thread","Blocks the calling thread","Cancels the task","await returns control to the caller and resumes when the awaited task finishes.")
M('a','k',"Why is calling .Result or .Wait() on a Task inside a UI or ASP.NET (classic) context risky?","It can cause a deadlock by blocking the context the continuation needs","It always throws","It makes the task run twice","It disables exceptions","Prefer await all the way. ConfigureAwait(false) helps in library code.")
M('a','k',"What does async void do differently from async Task?","Exceptions cannot be caught by the caller and the method cannot be awaited","It runs on a separate thread","It is faster","It returns a value","async void is meant for event handlers only. Use Task for everything else.")
M('a','k',"What does the lock statement do?","Allows only one thread at a time to run the block for the same lock object","Makes a variable read-only","Pauses all threads","Encrypts data","lock(obj) uses a monitor. Avoid locking on this or on public objects.")
topic('Types & Memory')
