M('a','k',"When does the garbage collector free an object?","When it is no longer reachable from any root, at a time the GC chooses","Immediately when the variable goes out of scope","When Dispose is called","Only when memory is full","Finalisation timing is non-deterministic, which is why IDisposable is used for resources like files and sockets.")
M('a','k',"What does Span<T> make possible?","Working with a slice of memory without copying or allocating","Running code in parallel","Locking a region of an array","Streaming over a network","Span<T> is a ref struct that lives on the stack, so it cannot be stored in a field of a normal class or captured by a lambda.")
M('a','k',"What is the difference between IEnumerable<T> and IQueryable<T>?","IQueryable builds an expression tree that a provider such as EF can translate, for example to SQL","IEnumerable is only for arrays","IQueryable cannot be filtered","They are identical","With IEnumerable the filtering happens in memory after all data is loaded.")
